### Which @angular/* package(s) are the source of the bug?

platform-server

### Is this a regression?

No

### Description

Relevant issue: https://github.com/angular/angular/issues/64175

Since Angular patches `globalThis` with `domino.impl`, node's `Event` and `CustomEvent` constructors are overwritten with non-intrinsic versions.

This causes issues for libraries like `p-queue`, which are implemented by extending `EventTarget`. When `p-queue` calls `this.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent())`, node throws a `TypeError`

```ts
import '@angular/compiler';
import { Component, provideZonelessChangeDetection } from '@angular/core';
import { bootstrapApplication } from '@angular/platform-browser';
import { renderApplication, provideServerRendering } from '@angular/platform-server';
import PQueue from 'p-queue';

class App {
  result = 'pending';

  constructor() {
    // p-queue 10 extends node's `EventTarget` and calls `this.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent(...))`.
    // Once Angular's server platform has installed domino's globals, `CustomEvent` is domino's
    // implementation, which node's `EventTarget#dispatchEvent` rejects.
    const queue = new PQueue({ concurrency: 1 });
    queue.add(() => 1);
    this.result = 'ok';
  }
}

Component({ selector: 'app-root', template: `<p>{{ result }}</p>` })(App);

const html = await renderApplication(
  (context) =>
    bootstrapApplication(
      App,
      { providers: [provideZonelessChangeDetection(), provideServerRendering()] },
      context,
    ),
  { document: '<html><body><app-root></app-root></body></html>' },
);
console.log(html);
```

### Please provide a link to a minimal reproduction of the bug

https://github.com/eblocha/angular-ssr-globals-clobbering

### Please provide the exception or error you saw

```true
TypeError [ERR_INVALID_ARG_TYPE]: The "event" argument must be an instance of Event. Received an instance of CustomEvent
```

